/*
Problem: 228. Summary Ranges
Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/summary-ranges/

-----------------------------------------------------

Problem Statement

Given a sorted unique integer array nums,
return the smallest sorted list of ranges that cover all numbers.

Each range should be:
- "a->b" if a != b
- "a" if a == b

-----------------------------------------------------

Pattern Used & Why

Pattern: Array Traversal (Range Expansion)

Why:
- Traverse once
- Expand consecutive sequence using while loop
- Store result when sequence breaks

-----------------------------------------------------

Key Idea

1. Start from current element
2. Expand while numbers are consecutive
3. Store range (single or multiple)
4. Continue

-----------------------------------------------------

Algorithm / Process

1. Loop through array
2. Mark start = nums[i]
3. Expand using while:
      nums[i] + 1 == nums[i+1]
4. End = nums[i]
5. Store:
      if start == end → "start"
      else → "start->end"

-----------------------------------------------------

Code
*/

import java.util.*;

class Solution {
    public List<String> summaryRanges(int[] nums) {

        List<String> res = new ArrayList<>();
        int n = nums.length;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {

            int start = nums[i];

            // expand consecutive range
            while (i < n - 1 && nums[i] + 1 == nums[i + 1]) {
                i++;
            }

            int end = nums[i];

            // add result
            if (start == end) {
                res.add(String.valueOf(start));
            } else {
                res.add(start + "->" + end);
            }
        }

        return res;
    }
}

/*
-----------------------------------------------------

Time Complexity
O(n)

-----------------------------------------------------

Space Complexity
O(1) (excluding output)

-----------------------------------------------------

Example

Input:
nums = [0,1,2,4,5,7]

Output:
["0->2", "4->5", "7"]

-----------------------------------------------------

Explanation :

Traverse array and expand consecutive elements using while loop.
Store ranges when sequence breaks.
*/
